-- THIS FILE IS MEANT TO FAIL. check.sh expects EXACTLY 3 failed assertions.
--
-- It is the SimpLEX test table of Figure 4, with the expectations the drafter
-- wrote for the draft, run unchanged against the Regulations as made on
-- 16 July 2025. Three of its six expectations no longer hold, which is what
-- a test suite that survives redrafting is for: the drafter would have seen
-- these go red the day the theoretical-examination fee was dropped and the
-- appeal fee attached to the practical examination alone.
--
-- Note what "run against the Regulations as made" now MEANS. There is no
-- vintage argument any more: the six rows below are the draft's expectations
-- asked of the ONE rule for regulation 2, with the rule-effective-time axis
-- pinned to the day the Regulations came into force. Swap the pinned date for
-- `the day the 5786 amendment came into force` and a different three rows go
-- red -- which is the argument for the axis. The draft's own expectations are
-- not on the axis and never were; they are the literal numbers the drafter
-- typed, carried here as expectations, exactly as a drafter's test file would
-- carry them forward through a redraft.
--
-- It doubles as the positive control for the tier 2 file: it proves the
-- harness CAN fail on this encoding.
@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-fees`

§ `The draft's expectations, against the Regulations as made`

-- #5  theoretical examination: fee 273                       -- FAILS: no fee was made
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `the day the Regulations came into force` (`the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`) EQUALS JUST 273
-- #6  practical examination: fee 194                          -- holds
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `the day the Regulations came into force` (`the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`) EQUALS JUST 194
-- #7  appeal against a practical examination score: 40        -- holds: (b) as made points at (a), the practical examination
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `the day the Regulations came into force` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a practical examination score`) EQUALS JUST 40
-- #7  appeal against a theoretical examination score: 40      -- FAILS: no theoretical examination in the text as made
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `the day the Regulations came into force` (`the fee prescribed for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) EQUALS JUST 40
-- #8  theoretical examination without payment: refused        -- FAILS: nothing to withhold
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `the day the Regulations came into force` (`the service may be provided` `theoretical examination` 0)
-- #8  practical examination without payment: refused          -- holds
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` `the day the Regulations came into force` (`the service may be provided` `practical examination` 0)
